 "equipment_type": "Water-cooled self-contained unit controller (IPU2)",
 "applies_to": "YORK L-Series LSWU, LSWD and LSWF water-cooled self-contained air conditioning units, 25-105 ton, with the IPU2 unit controller.",
 "summary": "The IPU2 controller of the L-Series water-cooled self-contained units speaks BACnet MS/TP on Port 1 (Modbus is also offered). The table lists about 170 objects: air and condenser water temperatures, refrigerant pressures, compressor and heat stage status, condenser water and waterside economizer valves, duct static and supply fan VFD values, setpoints and limits, BAS inputs, and BAS commands for occupancy, unit stop, morning warm-up, ventilation and heating.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "23000 + MAC address",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Access is from the READ/WRITE column; descriptions are the user interface names from the table. Points marked FlexSys, VAV or CV only exist on those units.",
  "The table prints ACT_SLAB_CTL (Modbus 1102) as AI 5 and COMFORT_VENT (Modbus 1103) as AI 2, the same IDs as the pressure points AV_PRS_A_SUC and AV_PRS_DIS; those two writable on/off rows are left out because their real object IDs cannot be told from the doc.",
  "The economizer method selector appears twice as AV 6 (ECONO_METHOD and ECON_METHOD); it is listed once. Ten on/off settings and commands (ECONO_INSTAL, FLSYS_REHEAT, HEAT_ENABLE, HEAT_VACTION, MORN_WARM_UP, MORN_WUP_CMD, NIGHT_SETBAC, OCCUPNCY_CMD, UNIT_STOP, VENT_ENABLE) are printed with both a BV and an AV ID (AV 81-95); they are listed by the BV ID.",
  "Multistate status codes (unit mode, system status, compressor status) are published as AIs; the code lists are in the table description column and are not repeated here.",
  "Units are taken from the description column where it states them. The Modbus register addresses in the same table are not reproduced.",
  "The older Versecon YSWU/YSWD IPU (IPU1) IOM 145.05-NOM3 prints a largely overlapping list."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "L-Series Water-Cooled Self-Contained Units Model LSWU/LSWD/LSWF with IPU2 Control, 25-105 Ton - Installation, Operation and Maintenance (Table 42, BACnet MS/TP, Modbus, BACnet IP)",
  "doc_number": "145.05-NOM7 (1019)",
  "revision_date": "2019-10-31",
  "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/ductedsystems/api/khub/documents/2clxIXbzWLHpg~aPscPCsA/content"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Connect to Port 1 of the IPU2 control board on BACnet MS/TP. Command occupancy with OCCUPNCY_CMD (BV 12), stop or release the unit with UNIT_STOP (BV 17) and write the occupied zone setpoints; read supply air, zone and condenser water temperatures, supply fan status, unit mode and the alarm input.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 12",
    "name": "OCCUPNCY_CMD",
    "why": "Occupancy command (1 = occupied)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 17",
    "name": "UNIT_STOP",
    "why": "Unit stop (1 = stopped, 0 = normal)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 21",
    "name": "OCC_ZN_COOL",
    "why": "Occupied zone cooling setpoint, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 22",
    "name": "OCC_ZN_HEAT",
    "why": "Occupied zone heating setpoint, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 58",
    "name": "UNIT_MODE",
    "why": "Current operating mode index"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 59",
    "name": "SUPPLY_FAN",
    "why": "Supply fan on/off"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 46",
    "name": "SUP_AIR_TEMP",
    "why": "Supply air temperature, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 60",
    "name": "ZONE_TEMP",
    "why": "Zone temperature, °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 90",
    "name": "WTR_TEMP_ENT",
    "why": "Entering condenser water temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 2",
    "name": "ALARM",
    "why": "Unit alarm (FLT = faulted)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "OCCUPNCY_CMD (BV 12) puts the unit in occupied (1) or unoccupied (0) mode and UNIT_STOP (BV 17) stops it (1) or returns it to normal operation (0). SYSTEM_STOP (AV 35) can turn off individual compressor systems.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": "ZONE_TMP_BAS (AV 40) lets the BAS supply zone temperature on a constant volume unit; OAT_CURR_BAS (AV 49) and OA_RH_BAS (AV 50) supply outdoor temperature and humidity when the airside economizer is selected; UND_TEMP_BAS / UND_HUMD_BAS (AV 37/36) feed under-floor values on FlexSys units.",
  "setup": [
   "BACnet MS/TP must use Port 1 of the IPU2 board; Port 2 is the RS-232 terminal port.",
   "Set the MAC address (1-127) with the SW2 DIP switches (switch 8 always ON) or the SERVICE key; the default device instance is 23000 plus the MAC address.",
   "A different device instance is set with DE MODIFIER ADDRESS x 100 + DE MODIFIER OFFSET; to keep the automatic instance, DE MODIFIER OFFSET must be -1.",
   "Cycle unit power after changing the MAC address or the port settings."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Setpoints, limits and enable values are setup values; don't write them cyclically.",
   "Many points only exist on FlexSys, VAV or constant volume units, or with options such as the waterside economizer."
  ]
 },
